# =========================================================
# BizGrow AI — environment variables
# =========================================================
# There are TWO separate places credentials go. Read this fully
# before deploying.
#
# 1) FRONTEND (public, safe to expose) — these go in js/config.js,
#    NOT in this .env file, because the site is static HTML/JS with
#    no build step. They are safe in the browser because Supabase's
#    anon key is protected by Row Level Security, not secrecy.
#
#      SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
#      SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
#
# 2) BACKEND (secret, server-side ONLY) — set these as Supabase Edge
#    Function secrets. NEVER put them in js/config.js, NEVER commit
#    them, NEVER send them to the browser.
#
#      supabase secrets set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
#      supabase secrets set AI_API_KEY=your-ai-provider-api-key
#      supabase secrets set AI_API_URL=https://api.your-ai-provider.com/v1/generate
#      supabase secrets set AI_MODEL=your-model-name
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY for the edge function are
# already injected automatically by the Supabase platform at runtime
# in most cases — check `supabase functions list` / your project's
# Edge Function settings if you need to set them explicitly.
# =========================================================
